"North of North Wellness Center for the Body and Mind is the fanciest gym in Apex."
"It is near the Celena North campus, and its name is written in logograms beside a crescent logo."
"It is a 'soft-super gym' whose clients are mostly off-duty Adjusters, Shapers and soft heroes."
"Three buildings joined by curving walkways sit among lawns and meditation gardens."
"Its menacing concrete building is covered in interface warnings over its one-ton kettlebells."
"Its elegant glass building has marble floors, a custom scent and a 4th-floor indoor track."
"It offers a free smoothie bar, potion-therapy saunas, a superolympic pool and a morphing course."
"Its medical center gives consultations and Celena North High entrance physicals."
"Membership costs a steep annual fee."
"Roberta 'Bobby', a D-rank Agility Brute, trains Alden there."
"Its morphable obstacle course of tough rubber reshapes walls, pillars, bars and puddles each run."
"The course room takes at most three people at once and is booked days ahead."
"Its showers have rainfall ceilings and attendants, with heated towels around lavender pouches."
"The smoothie bar has a frozen yogurt machine with seasonal flavors."
"The spa upstairs has a jellyfish aquarium wall between check-in and a robed lounge."
"Private relaxation rooms have heated lounge chairs and landscape screens over the garden."
"Famous heroes relax in the spa."
"It is ten minutes' walk from Celena North High's MagiPhys building, at the campus edge."
"A girl in lime yoga pants guards the entrance and hands out bottled liquefied salads."
"Its climbing wall can be set to high winds, floods or earthquakes."
"An onsite daycare has its own rock wall, and a 'heavy gym' serves professional heroes."
"Potion saunas cost 100 Argold or more; recovery potions can replace a rest day."
"The recovery sauna has two tiers of pale wood benches and a cauldron of watermelon potion."
"Sauna rules: shower first, towels only, no food, and no noisy, bright or smelly spells."
"Members observe a 'no bothering' policy toward one another."
"It also has a 'thought-softening sauna'."
"Its rich spa crowd is disproportionately likely to be summoned for dangerous work."
"It reopened with limited hours after the Matadero flood."
"It offers boxing classes; its climbing wall also has a landslide setting."
"Private training rooms pit members against an adaptive holographic attacker with live readouts."
"Members can buy guest passes; it has been busy since the floods."
